# Licensing

This repository contains both software and open hardware design files, which are
licensed differently.

Copyright (c) 2026 Jan Houwers.

## Firmware — MIT

Everything under `firmware/` is licensed under the **MIT License**.
Full text: [`LICENSES/MIT.txt`](LICENSES/MIT.txt).

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

## Hardware, CAD and documentation — CERN-OHL-S v2

Everything else — the CAD sources in `cad/`, the wiring diagrams in `hardware/`, and the
documentation in `docs/` and this README — is licensed under the
**CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 — Strongly Reciprocal**.
Full text: [`LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-v2.txt`](LICENSES/CERN-OHL-S-v2.txt).

SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-S-2.0

In short: you may use, study, modify and distribute these designs, and make and sell products
based on them, provided that you pass on the complete source of your modifications under the same
licence and keep the notices intact. See the licence text for the exact terms.

## Notice for products made from these designs

If you make or distribute a product based on this design, CERN-OHL-S v2 requires you to include a
notice. A suitable form:

```
This product is made from a design licensed under CERN-OHL-S v2:
https://github.com/JanHouwers/Brio-Train
Source available under CERN-OHL-S v2 at the above location.
```

## Disclaimer

These designs are provided **as is**, without warranty of any kind, and without any warranty of
fitness for a particular purpose or of non-infringement. Lithium-ion cells, chargers and motor
drivers can cause fire or injury if built or used incorrectly. You are responsible for verifying
the design and the safety of anything you build from it. See also the safety notes in
[`docs/assembly.md`](docs/assembly.md).

## Trademarks

BRIO is a trademark of BRIO AB. This is an independent, unaffiliated hobby project; the wheel and
coupler geometry is designed to be compatible with BRIO-style wooden track. No endorsement is
implied.
